HST Office: a print job disposes the printer it made for itself; each print job no longer keeps ~20 MB (vcl).

Each print job (vcl::PrinterController) without a printer makes its own: Printer::PreparePrintJob for the default
printer, the printer box of the print dialog and of the Print page's panel for each printer chosen. Nothing
disposed those printers, and vcl's list of printers (Printer::mpNext/mpPrev, ImplSVData::mpFirstPrinter) holds
every printer until it is disposed, so every job's printer stayed alive with its own font list: the font files
mapped again, about 20 MB per job. Opening the File panel's Print page makes a job each time, so the office grew by
about 20 MB per opening (Writer, Sheets, Slides alike). vcl::hst::JobPrinter now holds the printer the job made
(PrinterController::setPrinter, whose callers all make a new printer) and disposes it when the job chooses another
printer or ends. A printer given to the job's constructor (the old print API's VCLXPrinter, the document's
printer) stays its owner's.

Test: CppunitTest_vcl_hst_print_panel testJobPrinterEndsWithTheJob and testGivenPrinterStaysWithItsOwner;
tests/runtime/check-backstage-print-repeat.py checks the memory per opening after the warm-up.
